/-!
# Construction tools for the M₂₂ local shadow geometry

The contrary case is specified using an actual central-quotient equivalence
with M₂₂, the induced conjugation action, and a genuine Sz(2)/E₁₆ extension.
Automorphism coverage supplies the outer bound for every perfect central
cover. Once R₀ = 1 is established, this proves R = ⟨r⟩. The C₄-center
obstruction uses the symmetric outer action and the covering commutator
calculation.

With Q ≅ E₁₆ and the core placement and symmetry supplied, multiplication
constructs V = Q⟨r,z⟩ as an elementary group of order 64. Its canonical
binary vector space has dimension six. M and both local normalizers act
by the literal ambient conjugation maps, with the required centralizer
kernels. A crossed socle/radical criterion proves irreducibility from
actual invariant-subspace bounds.

The R₀/core-placement argument, outer symmetry, the local S₅ recognition,
and the intertwining and submodule calculations in the two center cases
remain unproved. The imported conditional constructions are not a proof
of those steps or of the outer exclusion in Lemma 16.4.7.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
proof of Lemma 16.4.7, printed p.1186 and the opening of p.1187.
-/
